Issue 063, logic only: stat allocation for unit templates. Nothing is drawn, and no one has seen this on a screen.

## Before
A template's stats could only be set by writing its data. There was no way to see what a change would cost, keep it within the limits and the budget, or get help spending the points.

## After
`src/editor/stat_allocator.lua` works on its own copy of a template.

- **`rows()`:** one row per stat, grouped as survival, mobility and awareness. Each row has:
  - the value and the body's own value;
  - the hard and comfortable limits;
  - the step size;
  - points paid, and the exact price before rounding up;
  - the cost of one more step and the saving from one fewer;
  - units per point;
  - the most the points left can buy;
  - the slider position.
- **Changing a stat:** `set`, `step`, `set_fraction` (snapped to the step) and `reset`. Each keeps the stat inside its limits and the budget, and says when it moved a value.
- **Six presets:** balanced, tank, bruiser, skirmisher, scout and spellguard. Each spends the points left by its shares.
- **`suggestions()`:**
  - over budget;
  - a stat below the body's own value;
  - a step already paid for by rounding;
  - unspent points;
  - one stat holding over 70% of the stat points.

## How
Costs come from the template's own breakdown and the prices in `template_costs.lua`, so the shown cost is the charged cost. Presets give one step at a time to the stat furthest below its share. A stat at its hard limit hands its share to the others.

## Decisions
- **Presets are shares of the points left, not the sketch's fixed values.** Fixed values ignore the body and the abilities already bought, and often land over budget.
- **Raising a stat is held to what the budget can buy.** Lowering is always allowed, so an over-budget template can always be brought back.
- **Values are whole numbers.** Buttons and sliders move by a step: 10 health, 5 speed or sight, 1 armor or magic resist.
- **The sketch's "expensive stat" advice is replaced** by advice the price model can back: points lost to rounding, and stats below the body's value.
- **Left unticked in the issue, because they need a screen:** the widgets, the visual feedback, drag and drop, and drawing the categories. Issue 063 moves to completed with these named.

## Tested
- `tests/test_stat_allocation.lua`, 6 tests:
  - rows match the charged costs;
  - limits and budget hold;
  - steps and sliders snap;
  - every preset on every body stays valid and in budget, and spends what it can;
  - each suggestion fires where it should;
  - the original template is untouched;
  - speed check.
- Passes under luajit and lua5.4.
- `./run <dir> unit`: the only ✗ is "LÖVE 2D not found".

Merge order: … #149 → #160 → this PR.

